  "instance_name": "snow_removal_stereotype",
  "label": "Snow Removal as Burdensome Labor",
  "description": "The meme relies on the real-world understanding that snow removal is a physically demanding and often tedious task, especially in regions with heavy snowfall. The humor stems from the absurdity of framing snow as an 'invasion' or 'intruder' on one's land, which is a metaphorical exaggeration of the real-world burden of winter maintenance. This stereotype is commonly associated with homeowners and property owners in snowy climates who must invest time and effort into clearing snow.",
